# Consistency First

Consistency beats novelty for both code and UX.

## Code

- Follow existing patterns; search before inventing new ones
- Reuse components/utils; extract when a pattern appears twice
- Match naming, file layout, API access, and state patterns already in the repo
- Prefer DRY — consolidate duplicate logic

## UI/UX

- Same colors, spacing, button variants/placement (Save right, Cancel left), form layout, breadcrumbs, cards/lists, URL shapes, hover/loading, and error display across pages
- Match styling of similar existing screens when adding UI

## Before Adding Code

1. Search for similar functionality
2. Reuse existing components/functions if they fit
3. Match styles of comparable UI
4. Follow established conventions elsewhere in the project
